WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.919
so the house judiciary committee has started
the process required to hold Donald Trump's

00:00:05.919 --> 00:00:06.919
attorney, right?

00:00:06.919 --> 00:00:07.919
Any General

00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:10.080
William Barr in contempt for the first question
is what?

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.080
What does that mean?

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.549
What does, what does it mean to be held in
contempt?

00:00:13.549 --> 00:00:20.300
In very simple terms, contempt is when somebody's
disobeys or ignores or disrespects the authority

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.019
of a duly empowered body.

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:27.220
Now, oftentimes we talk about being held in
contempt of court, but it also applies to

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.390
legislative bodies and is, in this particular
case, we're talking about Congress, contempt

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.660
of Congress, the House of Representatives.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:40.520
If you obstruct the legal work of Congress,
which includes ignoring subpoenas, not providing

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.980
documents, this can all be considered contempt
of congress and that's exactly what Democrats

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.690
are alleging or will allege that William Barr
did.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:56.360
He failed to comply with legal congressional
subpoenas when Congress requested the unredacted

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.110
Robert Mueller report and William Barr didn't
provide it.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:06.229
Now this would just be step one, a of the
process of actually holding bar and contempt.

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:09.640
And I don't think that's a process that will
ever actually be followed through to its full

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.640
conclusion.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:11.870
And I'll explain that in a moment.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:17.219
But step one is for the committee to vote
on this, uh, tomorrow, Wednesday.

00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:24.229
Now it's important to know that even though
bar released the redacted report, the unredacted

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:26.350
reports still has not been released.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:32.100
And Chairman of the House Judiciary Committee,
Jerry Nadler says he'd consider postponing

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:37.749
tomorrow's vote on a contempt against bar
if bar gives them the full on redacted report.

00:01:37.749 --> 00:01:40.569
No indication right now that that's actually
going to happen.

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:44.630
But the most interesting thing about this
is not the specifics of getting the unredacted

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:45.630
report.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.850
I think they should have the unredacted report.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:55.319
The most interesting thing about this is not
whether bar will actually be held in contempt

00:01:55.319 --> 00:01:56.679
because I don't think he will.

00:01:56.679 --> 00:01:58.539
And I'll tell you why in a second.

00:01:58.539 --> 00:02:04.990
What's riveting about this is that this is,
uh, this contempt of Congress charge was one

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:09.920
of the three things in the articles of impeachment
against Richard Nixon back in 1974.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:16.930
I told you last week that Trump 2019 is looking
more and more like Nixon 1974 and yesterday

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:23.350
on the show I did a story outlining how the
difference between 2019 and 1974 isn't that

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:26.980
what Nixon did is worse than what Trump has
done.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:33.280
It's that Republicans in the 70s drew the
line at abuses of power of this level even

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.870
by people in their party.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.390
Republicans in 2019, on the other hand don't
care about that.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.830
They have no such line.

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:43.240
So that is why this is so interesting.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:49.820
But to get back to the contempt itself, um,
contempt of Congress against a sitting attorney

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:57.990
general is unlikely to ever actually be carried
fully out because, uh, when think to what

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:02.790
Libertarians always talk about, they say the
government is an initiator of force because

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.930
eventually men with guns will come for you.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.470
Doesn't sound like taxation is a, uh, some
kind of slavery under duress.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:15.290
Well if you don't pay your taxes eventually
men with guns show up.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.271
That actually is a relevant thing to think
about when it comes to contempt of Congress

00:03:18.271 --> 00:03:23.000
against William Barr because if the house
